2026-02-11 02:39:49,228 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document The Bottom Line

An asset class is a grouping of investments that exhibit similar characteristics and that may be subject to the same rules and regulations. Equities, fixed income, commodities, and real estate are common examples of asset classes.

Asset classes can be used to diversify portfolios and reduce risk, as each class typically reflects different risk and return characteristics. Building a portfolio with asset classes that are not highly correlated with one another is an important concept for successful diversification. is relevant
